@buena mole wrote:

>Maybe for good reason people are becoming slightly more health conscious except that 40% of the population is obese, eating ultra-processed food served at subsidized prices so we eat a lot!

One thing I've noticed is that whole wheat pasta has become much harder to find. Just a few years ago, it seemed to be stocked almost everywhere and sold for about $1 a pound. Now it's difficult to find. So when I found 100% whole wheat penne on sale online, I bought several cases.
